lines=['# Remaining48: first13accepted CH points, closed program/kernel evidence','', '**Fixed as-of:** 2026-11-04 09:45:49 Asia/Shanghai (01:45:49UTC), source-qualified snapshot20261104T014550071642Z_5263ab47. This analysis intentionally freezes that snapshot even if the live provider advances. It covers13/48new CH points across10/24new programs, with3new programs complete in bothF profiles. Overall CORE32 common coverage at this snapshot is11/32, including the already completed first8. No partial GM is computed or presented as a CORE32 conclusion.','', '**Findings:** twelve matched CH/DH F comparisons are exact zero response within each design, down to every captured kernel cycle and the selected final additive counters. Six programs have0issued DRAM reads/writes and0controller requests across all consumed closed profiles. Their nonzero all-L2 misses, where present, are GLOBAL writes rather than read misses. The sole nonzero newly matched case is fastWalshTransform-F128: CH improves418cycles, DH regresses65cycles. Both have identical DRAM volume and fewer retry/admission events; the phase decomposition shows opposing stage movements.','', 'The closed sample is dominated by short jobs that finished first, not a new benchmark selection. Every planned input remains in the consumer\'s fixed32population, and missing CH counterparts remain pending rather than inferred from old DH data. No source, model, dispatcher/owner, registry, input, budget or v0.23 manuscript is modified.','', '## All thirteen newly closed comparisons','',tab(['Program','F','CH0','CH_F','DH0','DH_F','S_CH','S_DH','CH_F/DH_F','I'],[[x['program'],x['profile'],by[x['program'],'CH','P0']['cycles'],by[x['program'],'CH',x['profile']]['cycles'],by[x['program'],'DH','P0']['cycles'],by[x['program'],'DH',x['profile']]['cycles'],*[x['metrics'][k]for k in['S_CH','S_DH','R','I']]]for x in comp]),'', 'The fastWalsh DH-F128 sign is retained as measured (S_DH0.999649, cycle increase0.0351%); it is neither discarded as noise nor promoted to a gain. Its CH speedup is1.002185 and I0.997470. The original DH-F256 point185,740cycles is separately available, but new CH-F256 is pending in this snapshot, so no matched F256 I is claimed.','', '## Program/kernel scope and source-derived interpretation','',tab(['Program / full input identity','Observed launches and unique symbols','Source-candidate behavior','Measured scope/limit'],[[x['program']+' / '+x['input_digest'],str(x['observed_kernel_count'])+'; '+'; '.join(k+':'+str(v)for k,v in x['observed_unique_symbols_counts'].items()),x['candidate_source_description'],x['runtime_observation_or_limit']]for x in facts]),'', 'Program descriptions are fixed Atlas candidate-source deductions, not capture ELF/numeric certification or measured cache-hit/merge behavior. Runtime names/order/instruction contracts and all cycles were independently matched to the actual frozen body qualification. Source reports at Atlas47a097aad4406893a07f8d230e1e0a850609bf39, their Git paths/SHA and exact per-program provenance limits are preserved in FIXED_ATLAS_REPORT_BINDINGS.json and fixed_atlas_reports/. They are not reintroduced as a new generic source survey.','', '## Why all-L2 miss does not imply DRAM-read pressure','',tab(['Program','CH0 GLOBAL read misses32B','CH0 all-L2 misses32B','Nonzero CH0 miss access types','All consumed profiles DRAM_R/W/n_req zero','Observed HtoD count / bytes'],[[x['program'],x['CH_P0_global_read_misses'],x['CH_P0_all_L2_misses'],str(x['CH_P0_type_misses']),x['all_consumed_closed_profiles_DRAM_R_W_n_req_zero'],str(x['CH_P0_runtime_HtoD_copies'])+' / '+str(x['CH_P0_runtime_HtoD_bytes'])]for x in types]),'', 'BlackScholes25,000, histogram7,752, mergeSort4,128 and dwt2d27,648all-L2 miss sectors are explicitly GLOBAL_ACC_W, while GLOBAL read misses and issued DRAM data requests are0. Gaussian/lud have no measured L2 misses or DRAM data requests. This is a counted access-type distinction, not missing counters treated as zero. All53closed sources conserve the per-type MISS+SECTOR_MISS sum against the all-L2 miss total.','', 'The actual fixed L2 string `S:128:128:16,L:B:m:L:L,A:192:4,32:0,32` selects write-back plus LAZY_FETCH_ON_READ. Fixed Core9eed `gpu-cache.h:696-712;1610-1626` maps this option to `wr_miss_wa_lazy_fetch_on_read`; `gpu-cache.cc:1858-1922` marks writes dirty/valid and returns MISS without an ordinary read fetch, with writeback conditional on a dirty eviction. This provides a source-established reason a counted write miss need not produce a DRAM read. It does not identify every individual event\'s dynamic path or prove application stores/dirty cache data were absent. Issued write0is not a complete eventual dirty-data drain guarantee.','', 'Every closed raw prints the exact frozen ordered MemcpyHtoD/kernel commands; all53command lists were checked, not assumed from file names. The actual options retain perf_sim_memcpy=1 and flush_l2_cache=0. Fixed Framework/Core code routes those copies through32-byte `force_l2_tag_update`/tag fill without ordinary timed host-transfer DRAM traffic. This establishes the active replay prefill policy; reuse during kernels and across kernels can also contribute. It does not certify all data residence, original numerical input or real-GPU warm/cold behavior. CONSUMED_MEMCPY_SOURCE_EVIDENCE.json retains exact source commit/path/SHA/line witnesses.','', 'These six measured replays do not exercise an issued DRAM data-request window under this fixed sampled condition. They must not be called compute-bound, nor used to generalize that L2/DRAM resources never matter to their larger/other inputs. In particular, histogram still reports CH341,933 / DH395,635 ICNT blocked-admission events despite DRAM_R/W/n_req0. The legacy label `gpu_stall_dramfull` is an ICNT-to-subpartition admission-event counter, not isolated DRAM queue time or critical-path duration.','', '## fastWalshTransform: opposite stage responses','', 'The actual16kernel sequence is12global fwtBatch2,3shared terminal fwtBatch1,1modulate. For both CH and DH, K1-K5 cycle counts are unchanged across the matched P0/F128 run. All65,280issued read atoms (2,088,960bytes) and all visible L2 retries occur in the K6 print interval. Later kernel cycles can still move even with0new issued DRAM reads in their intervals; a zero-current-traffic phase is not proof of timing/history independence. These are completed-kernel print intervals, not guaranteed request-origin labels.','',tab(['K','Actual symbol','CH0','CH128','CHdelta','DH0','DH128','DHdelta','CH0/128 DRAM read atoms in interval'],[[k['ordinal'],k['kernel'],k['cycles'],by['fastWalshTransform','CH','F128']['kernels'][k['ordinal']-1]['cycles'],by['fastWalshTransform','CH','F128']['kernels'][k['ordinal']-1]['cycles']-k['cycles'],by['fastWalshTransform','DH','P0']['kernels'][k['ordinal']-1]['cycles'],by['fastWalshTransform','DH','F128']['kernels'][k['ordinal']-1]['cycles'],by['fastWalshTransform','DH','F128']['kernels'][k['ordinal']-1]['cycles']-by['fastWalshTransform','DH','P0']['kernels'][k['ordinal']-1]['cycles'],str(k['print_interval_additive']['DRAM_read_atoms32B'])+'/'+str(by['fastWalshTransform','CH','F128']['kernels'][k['ordinal']-1]['print_interval_additive']['DRAM_read_atoms32B'])]for k in by['fastWalshTransform','CH','P0']['kernels']]),'',tab(['Design','Candidate phase','P0 cycles','F128 cycles','Delta'],[[c,phase,next(g['cycles']for x in wg if x['cell']==c and x['profile']=='P0'for g in x['groups']if g['phase_candidate']==phase),next(g['cycles']for x in wg if x['cell']==c and x['profile']=='F128'for g in x['groups']if g['phase_candidate']==phase),next(g['cycles']for x in wg if x['cell']==c and x['profile']=='F128'for g in x['groups']if g['phase_candidate']==phase)-next(g['cycles']for x in wg if x['cell']==c and x['profile']=='P0'for g in x['groups']if g['phase_candidate']==phase)]for c in['CH','DH']for phase in['global_radix4','shared_terminal_transform','modulate']]),'', 'CH cycle delta=-507global +148shared -59modulate =-418. DH delta=-151global +295shared -79modulate =+65. Thus a small global-pass gain coexists with a larger shared-terminal-pass regression in DH. Candidate fwtBatch1 uses shared staging/barriers; this is a source characteristic, not proof that shared-memory/barrier service caused the measured regression. Changed timing/order/clock alignment/history are hypotheses until a critical-path observation establishes a cause.','', 'CH L2 retries147,110 ->133,311 and ICNT admission events688,493 ->676,494 fall. DH retries127,552 ->115,953 and admission639,783 ->623,587 also fall, yet DH total cycles increase. DH OO lower creations265,674 ->265,624 and valid-line hits12,854 ->12,904 conserve278,528classified line probes, with accepted sectors=4*128B lower creations. These small improvements in selected counters do not imply a faster end-to-end execution.','', 'DH finite-service ready-to-complete sum678,914 ->680,234 and writeback wait51,672 ->52,289 rise slightly; these are aggregate entry/sample measures, not critical-path cycles. Reported MRQ115 ->198(CH)/199(DH) increases while mflatency1123 ->1114(CH),1168 ->1161(DH) slightly decreases. Means have distinct denominators and known print/update/tail windows; the final dictionary is not an exact per-kernel or full-app mean. Do not subtract/sum means or read missing latency as0. No proof that average complete L2-to-DRAM critical-load latency fell is available.','', '## Facts, correlations and unresolved cause','', '- Facts:12zero paired responses include identical per-kernel cycles/selected additive totals; six programs have explicitly0DRAM requests; FWT has one cold/read-active print interval and mixed later phase deltas. All source RESULT/raw gzip/raw plain/input-binding/exit hashes and actual kernel contracts were checked.','- Source deductions: fixed replay memcpy prefill, active lazy-write policy, and per-kernel algorithm/control descriptions; capture source/ELF/original numerical completeness remains bounded by each frozen report.','- Correlations: FWT counters for retries/OO misses improve while its DH cycles regress slightly; zero-response cases coincide with little/no DRAM request volume. Neither association identifies a critical path.','- Unconfirmed: bank/credit occupancy, request age, pipeline/barrier/issue/finite-service criticality and causal timing history. Current means/retry counts are not occupancy or stall-time attribution. No new instrumentation, rerun or combination is started.','', 'CH PAPER_BASE common PIB256 and DH PAPER_OO PIB128 remain explicitly separate; generic DH PIB8 does not set OO admission. Unprinted OO PIB-full/Tag-conflict fields stay null and are not populated with CH zeros. Cross-design L1/Tag/physical pool/queues/timing/area differences remain. FR-FCFS64/128/256 also changes shared-credit limits255/319/447, while DRAM850MHz and10MiB L2 stay fixed. This is a coupled-window/credit study, not free equal-area hardware.','', '## Evidence and reproducibility','', 'Authority5f67b4d6b94568a9f1acc80c3e56736bd81e4753 and fixed identity plan5001c3f35052f7f91f1ad41eeff83f2947a0878d remain unchanged. Runtime Core9eedb3131937748f0492fa83aad37d3691118d70 / Framework02775fd795cde5aae1480d81cee6eb481d0a08f4 / binary02a289360b42a573832698c978f21ad2125182a453067a35be60410f1eb8888d are verified across all53closed sources. SOURCE_SNAPSHOT_RECEIPT.json pins the exact qualified snapshot manifest1292c386ef93ba0a49772b608a13310fe772db77611f769cc0082c0c35ea9a80, observed provider pointer SHA, source-qualified counts and all compressed file hashes.','', 'CLOSED_SOURCE_KERNEL_COUNTERS.json.gz holds all53RESULT/raw/exit/input-binding paths/SHA, UUIDs, roles, every actual kernel name/instruction/cycle/raw-line boundary, explicit additive intervals, retry reasons and command invocations. MATCHED_COMPARISONS.json includes all13paired signs/zeros and every kernel cycle delta. TYPE_MISS_AND_INITIAL_STATE.json and TYPED_FRONTEND_SERVICE.json retain access-type/domain distinctions. WALSH_PHASE_GROUPS.json preserves candidate grouping. Fixed source semantics/catalog and175+173=348passing evidence checks are separate files. No live raw was read or copied into Git.','', 'The frozen default script does not overwrite a published MANIFEST. For a later naturally closed qualified snapshot, use the same entry with `--provider <official_PUBLICATION_PROVIDER.json> --output-dir <this_dir>/updates/<new_tag>`; it writes a new child, retaining all then-accepted counterparts and pending coverage without altering reader/native files. This is a callable analysis entry, not another daemon or model controller. New source-candidate claims require review; no absent F counterpart or mechanistic counter is inferred.','',tab(['Program','Profile','Role','RESULT path','RESULT SHA256'],[[x['program'],x['cell']+'-'+x['profile'],x['source_role'],x['RESULT_path'],x['RESULT_sha256']]for x in data]),'']
